„­bible_version£KJV¤book#§chapter¨sections™…¤book#§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses’„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ?Woe to her that is filthy and polluted, to the oppressing city!¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙqShe obeyed not the voice; she received not correction; she trusted not in the LORD; she drew not near to her God.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book#§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses“„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙqHer princes within her are roaring lions; her judges are evening wolves; they gnaw not the bones till the morrow.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ|Her prophets are light and treacherous persons: her priests have polluted the sanctuary, they have done violence to the law.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ£The just LORD is in the midst thereof; he will not do iniquity: every morning doth he bring his judgment to light, he faileth not; but the unjust knoweth no shame.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book#§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses’„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¼I have cut off the nations: their towers are desolate; I made their streets waste, that none passeth by: their cities are destroyed, so that there is no man, that there is none inhabitant.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¹I said, Surely thou wilt fear me, thou wilt receive instruction; so their dwelling should not be cut off, howsoever I punished them: but they rose early, and corrupted all their doings.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book#§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses‘„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÚ%Therefore wait ye upon me, saith the LORD, until the day that I rise up to the prey: for my determination is to gather the nations, that I may assemble the kingdoms, to pour upon them mine indignation, even all my fierce anger: for all the earth shall be devoured with the fire of my jealousy.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book#§chapter«first_verse	ªlast_verse
