¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙoFrom beyond the rivers of Ethiopia my suppliants, even the daughter of my dispersed, shall bring mine offering.¦layout ªlast_verse
…¤book#§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses“„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙöIn that day shalt thou not be ashamed for all thy doings, wherein thou hast transgressed against me: for then I will take away out of the midst of thee them that rejoice in thy pride, and thou shalt no more be haughty because of my holy mountain.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙrI will also leave in the midst of thee an afflicted and poor people, and they shall trust in the name of the LORD.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¹The remnant of Israel shall not do iniquity, nor speak lies; neither shall a deceitful tongue be found in their mouth: for they shall feed and lie down, and none shall make them afraid.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book#§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses’„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙkSing, O daughter of Zion; shout, O Israel; be glad and rejoice with all the heart, O daughter of Jerusalem.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ£The LORD hath taken away thy judgments, he hath cast out thine enemy: the king of Israel, even the LORD, is in the midst of thee: thou shalt not see evil any more.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book#§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses’„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙdIn that day it shall be said to Jerusalem, Fear thou not: and to Zion, Let not thine hands be slack.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ The LORD thy God in the midst of thee is mighty; he will save, he will rejoice over thee with joy; he will rest in his love, he will joy over thee with singing.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book#§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses“„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙxI will gather them that are sorrowful for the solemn assembly, who are of thee, to whom the reproach of it was a burden.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÒBehold, at that time I will undo all that afflict thee: and I will save her that halteth, and gather her that was driven out; and I will get them praise and fame in every land where they have been put to shame.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÑAt that time will I bring you again, even in the time that I gather you: for I will make you a name and a praise among all people of the earth, when I turn back your captivity before your eyes, saith the LORD.¦layout ªlast_verse